analysis:
Integration pass over CI-only changes: .github/actions/provider-ci-build/action.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, .github/workflows/docs-impact.yml, docs (docs/developer/build.md, changelog.d/ci-git-swiftpm-cache.md) and offline tests (scripts/test-*.py). None touch provider runtime, the coordinator WebSocket (TB-002), App Attest authorization (TB-011), keys, attestation or the prefix cache (T-041, which concerns the runtime KV cache and not CI caches). No provider asset or threat-model control is weakened.

Direction of change is hardening. Cache saves are gated by SAVE_CACHES (push to master or dev only) and by the action's save-caches input, which defaults to 'false' (action.yml lines 7-9, 107, 116, 143), so PR code cannot write caches that trusted runs restore. Checkouts use persist-credentials:false, so the job token is not stored in a cached .git/config. The .git save step runs right after checkout and before PR code executes. Actions are SHA-pinned and no untrusted input is interpolated into scripts. The new SwiftPM repositories cache is restore-only on PRs, with keys bound to OS, layout, lane and the Package.resolved hash.

Docs-impact.yml adds blob:none and a sparse checkout that excludes only .gz evidence archives and .mp4 videos. Permissions and the checked-out ref are unchanged. Tests assert the fail-closed cold-checkout fallback; only the cached checkout may set continue-on-error.

Unverified, because the replay covered only 39 units and the full ci.yml head and the head side of test-provider-ci-workflow.py were not wholly visible:
(1) every save step in ci.yml is gated on SAVE_CACHES. unit 2 saw this at the cited lines, but that was not independently replayed in full;
(2) a restored stale .git does not feed outdated refs to release-integrity or provenance scripts such as check-release-version.sh;
(3) the without_cached_checkout helper strips only the intended step;
(4) the Darkbloom sandbox plane's push admission is an external contract.
No concrete regression is established, so findings are empty. A later pass could confirm (1)-(3) against the full ci.yml.
